<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>A Helping Hand</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Soviet Union&amp;nbsp;vs. United States&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;/FONT&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/STRONG&gt; 25th May, 1979/ 06:00:00 Zulu&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Location:&lt;/STRONG&gt; Midway Island&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Duration:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;1.5 Days&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;United States&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Since the start of hostilities Midway Island has been reinforced with additional equipment including Hawk SAM and a Squadron of fighters from Hawaii.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Soviets are after a "stepping stone" in the Pacific and Midway Island is a ripe target, with limited Naval assets in the vicinity the US has called on its allies to assist.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;With luck a combined UK and Canadian Task Group have been operating in the region when hostilities started, the group is centred around HMS Queen Elizabeth CVA which was commisioned 4 years earlier.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;With her Airgroup and escorts she should be able to defend Midway.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Paul Bridge&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Author and Scenario Designer&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Authors Note&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;HMS Queen Elizabeth CVA-01 was cancelled at the design stage due to the defence cuts in the UK in the 1960's.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
